I've played these games on and off for the last couple of years
here in London.  According to the January 1993 (Issue One)
*Black Ice*, the machines are designed and manufactured in the
UK by W Industries, the brainchild of Dr. Jon Waldern.  Other
games based on the same hardware include:

1.) Heavy Metal
        One of my favorites.  2-4 players are networked into the
        same virtual battlefield, where each commands a "walker"
        style weapons platform, reminiscent of the faster bipeds
        employed against rebel ground forces in Lucasfilm's *The
        Empire Strikes Back".

        As with most of these games, the point is to shoot The
        Other Guy.

